        "original_id": "907253a6-2936-54fb-9e6c-8aaf1648ee30",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Pascoe St Leger Grenfell\n- Organizations: South Australian Church Society, Trinity City\n- Places: North Terrace, Adelaide\n- Buildings: Holy Trinity Church\n\nFacts:\n- Pascoe St Leger Grenfell was a valued committee member of the South Australian Church Society.\n- Pascoe St Leger Grenfell donated an acre of land on North Terrace in Adelaide for the construction of Holy Trinity Church.\n- Holy Trinity Church was one of the first churches built in the city of Adelaide and in the colony.\n- Trinity City holds four gatherings at the North Terrace location each Sunday.\n- Trinity City also holds various other meetings throughout the week at the North Terrace location.",
